        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Rain drummed harder beyond the workshop, and wind pushed damp air through the wide gate. Mert stood squarely in the approach, maintaining the boundary he had already set. The restored mosaic panel rested nearby, intact, its fitted pieces bright against the grey afternoon.\n\nAya studied it with growing impatience. “I can carry the panel alone,” she said. “If I’m careful, we’ll get it there faster.”\n\nMert looked directly at Aya as she made the proposal, then glanced at the fragile panel without shifting from the gate approach.\n\n“No,” he said, calm but firm. “The safe route starts through this wide gate, and I’m keeping the boundary here until we’re ready for a proper shared carry. From the gate, the route stays under cover across the yard. Then it follows the level covered ramp to the gallery entry and goes through the wide open gallery door.”\n\nAya listened, her gaze following the direction he described even though neither of them left the workshop.\n\nMert continued, “There’s no reason to rush the first part and risk the whole panel. The rain is getting stronger, but the route itself is covered. We need to use it carefully.”\n\nFor a moment, Aya’s mouth tightened. She looked again at the same restored panel, still resting where it had been. Then she gave a reluctant nod.\n\n“All right,” she said. “I understand the covered route.”\n\nMert saw her acknowledgment and accepted it without stepping away from the gate approach. The boundary remained in place. Aya did not ask him for help—not yet—but she no longer argued for taking an uncovered shortcut or denied the route he had explained.",
